{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>וַיַּעַשׂ מֹשֶׁה כַּאֲשֶׁר וְגוֹ׳ כֵּן עָשָׂה.</b> The reason he repeated the matter is that it further intends this: <b>וַיַּעַשׂ כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳</b> etc. — meaning, immediately and without delay when He commanded him, he did not tarry. <b>כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳</b> — meaning, to answer that thus he did; and accordingly the word <b>כַּאֲשֶׁר</b> is drawn both upward (to what precedes) and downward (to what follows)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:46.107528818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}